- **Bug found by the eval: Chroma HNSW misses the small docs.** Not crowding: an exact cosine search ranks the right `services_fees.pdf` chunk at 0.846, but `collection.query` returns six `bsb.txt` chunks at ~0.55, even with `ef_search` raised to 2000 (> 5,067 vectors). `count()` includes the small docs' vectors, but the HNSW search never returns them. The fees and CELPIP docs were indexed before `bsb.txt`. Filtered (`--scope doc`) queries are fine. Chroma 1.5.9. Explains the M3 "Found" note. Next: reproduce in a small script (index order, `sync_threshold`), check Chroma issues, try a newer Chroma or a re-add; hybrid BM25 (M5) would hide it but not fix it
  - Repro script `eval/hnsw_repro.py` (2026-10-21, free, no LLM). `existing` (copy of the eval index): 17/31 answerable questions lose the target doc from the top 6 with **no filter too**, so the `$in` filter isn't the cause. Self-recall (query each stored vector with itself): `bsb.txt` 4978/4978, `services_fees.pdf` 59/82, CELPIP **0/7**. Collection config: `ef_search` 100, `max_neighbors` 16, `sync_threshold` 1000, `resize_factor` 1.2
  - `synthetic` (clustered random vectors, plain chromadb, 64-vector upserts): small docs first → recall@6 0.78; small first + delete-before-upsert → 0.89; big doc first → 0.97. Same in a fresh process. So it depends on index order and happens without any app code
  - Re-add workaround (2026-10-21, `existing --readd delete|upsert [--ef-search N] [--reopen]`): writing the small docs' vectors again after `bsb.txt` (delete + add, or upsert in place) → self-recall 100% for all three docs, questions missing the target doc 17/31 → 1–2/31 (celpip-06/07, varies run to run). Re-add + `ef_search` 400 or 2000 → **0/31**, also from a fresh process. `ef_search` 2000 alone → still 17/31. Synthetic: re-add → recall 0.96–1.0 (vs 0.78–0.88 small-first; synthetic numbers vary ±0.1 between runs)
  - So vectors written while the collection was small are left badly linked once it grows; writing them again repairs the links. Not a fix for the app (any small doc indexed before a big one is hit)
  - Other chromadb versions (2026-10-21): 1.5.9 is the newest on PyPI (no pre-releases), so bisected older ones in throwaway venvs instead. `dump` (backend venv) saves the eval index's real vectors + question embeddings to `eval/output/hnsw_dump.npz`; `replay` (numpy + chromadb only) re-indexes them like the pipeline. Small docs first: CELPIP self-recall **0/7 on 1.0.21, 1.3.7 and 1.5.9**, fees 45–78/82, 6–14/31 questions miss (varies per run). Reversed order: all 100%, 1–2/31 miss (celpip-06/07). Not a regression in 1.x; 0.6.3 (pre-Rust hnswlib) wouldn't install (`chroma-hnswlib` needs C++ build tools on py3.12/Windows)
  - Chroma issues searched (2026-10-21). **#2250** (closed 2025-01 for inactivity, 0.4.24) is the same bug: small doc then 100k-chunk doc → small-doc queries return the big doc at ~0.55, re-adding the small doc fixes it. A maintainer asked for the embeddings to debug; closed with "open a new issue if it still happens on ≥0.6.0 and raising `search_ef` doesn't help" — both now true. Related, open: #7758 (1.5.9, live records unreachable after deletes/upserts; disconnected-node mechanism) with PR #7845 (exact-search fallback for fragmented indexes; triggered by deletes, so may not cover ours). Also #3580, #1737/#620 (older recall reports), #3486 (HNSW master issue)
  - Chroma issue filed (2026-10-26): **chroma-core/chroma#7963**, references #2250 and #7758, real-data counts only (no names or embeddings), version table, standalone repro `eval/chroma_issue_repro.py` (chromadb + numpy, ~30 s; small first 80–109/120 and 35/40 found, `ef_search` 2000 no better, re-upsert 120/120 and 40/40)
  - Watch #7963 for a fix or a maintainer request (2026-10-26: open, no replies); when a fixed chromadb ships, re-run `eval/hnsw_repro.py` and drop `rebuild-index` from the README tip if it's no longer needed
  - App-side workaround (2026-10-26, branch `m2-hnsw-rebuild`): `python -m app.ingestion.cli rebuild-index [--check]` (`pipeline.rebuild_index()`) upserts every document's stored vectors, texts and metadata again, largest document first, no re-embedding; `--check` prints per-doc self-recall (`pipeline.index_recall()`) before and after. Eval index copy: 13 s; self-recall with `ef_search` 400 alone fees 77/82, CELPIP 1/7 → after rebuild 82/82, 7/7, bsb 4978/4978
