## Agentic redesign (decided 2026-10-16; loop built 2026-10-19 behind `QA_MODE=agent`; UI steps, docs and eval done 2026-10-21 on branch `agentic-redesign`)

Change from a fixed RAG pipeline (one Claude call per question) to an agent loop where Claude decides what to search, reads results, and searches again before answering. Do this before M4: streaming, history and follow-ups all build on the query path.

- **Step 1: QA tracing** (2026-10-16, branch `qa-tracing`, commit `6ece292`) (so the current pipeline is measurable and the agent loop is traceable from day one). Today only the question, final answer, verified claims and groundedness are saved, and the question is lost when the answer fails (409/503)
  - `qa_traces` table, one row per question including failures: conversation + message ids, timestamp, question, `doc_filter`, settings used (`top_k`, `min_relevance`, `strict_mode`, model), retrieved chunks with score + rank, gate decision, raw Claude JSON before verification, per-claim verification (exact/fuzzy, score, original vs corrected label), outcome, final response, error, tokens in/out, latency per stage (retrieve / LLM / verify)
  - `qa_trace_steps` child table for the agent loop: one row per step (tool call + input, results returned, model text), in order. Table and API exist; the pipeline writes no steps, the agent loop will
  - Save the user question even when answering fails (also sets the title). Retrying from the UI after an error now leaves the failed question in the history too
  - Store `outcome` on the assistant message, so the UI stops inferring it from claims (`outcomeOf`)
  - One JSON log line per question: ids, outcome, timings, tokens. No question text or document content in stdout logs (traces stay in the local DB only: privacy, §2.3)
  - `GET /api/conversations/{id}/traces` (with steps)
  - "Show reasoning" panel in the UI (2026-10-21): the collapsible steps list under each agent answer (see the UI item below). Raw traces are still at `GET /api/conversations/{id}/traces`
  - Schema change: existing SQLite DBs need the new table/column (`create_all` doesn't alter tables): add a small migration step or document a reset. Done: `init_db` adds missing nullable columns listed in `ADDED_COLUMNS` (`db/session.py`); checked on a copy of the local DB
  - Unit tests: trace written on verified / not-found / unsupported / LLM error / no documents
- Update the design doc (2026-10-21, v2.3): §2.3 data boundary (agent mode sends every chunk it reads), new §6.2 agent mode, §7 layers 1–2 + §7.3 (verifies against every chunk seen), §9 API (rename/delete/list/traces, `steps` in replies, agent `status` SSE event), §10 `AnswerMessage` steps, §11.1 `QA_MODE` + `AGENT_*`, §12 runner location and metrics, §16 agentic redesign row, Appendix D (changes + eval results)
- Decide the loop implementation: LangChain `ChatAnthropic.bind_tools` with our own loop (matches `llm.py`, full control over limits and verification) vs LangGraph / `create_agent`. Chose our own loop (`generation/agent.py`)
- Read-only tools: `search_documents(query, doc_ids?, k)` (returns labelled excerpts `C#` + scores), `list_documents()`, `read_chunk(doc_id, idx)` / neighbouring chunks. No tool with side effects
- Limits: max tool calls per question (start ~5), wall-clock timeout, token cap; on hitting a limit answer from what was found or return not-found. Never forced `tool_choice` (use `auto` + prompt)
- Final answer stays `GroundedAnswer` (structured). Built as the pipeline's grounded prompt over every excerpt the agent collected (a structured call on the tool transcript would need tools + structured output in one call; see agentic_ai.md §3 Step 4). Excerpt labels are unique across the whole loop; quote verification runs against every chunk the agent saw, same rules as now (`verification/quotes.py`, `STRICT_MODE`)
- Relevance gate: replaced by scores in tool results + the model's not-found; keep a hard stop when no search returns anything above `MIN_RELEVANCE`
- Prompt injection: tool results are document text: keep the excerpts-are-data rule in the system prompt and in each tool result wrapper
- `QA_MODE=agent|pipeline` setting, keep the current pipeline for comparison and as a fallback. Settings + `AGENT_*` limits in `config.py`, `.env.example` (2026-10-16); switch in `qa.py` (2026-10-19)
- Design write-up: [agentic_ai.md](agentic_ai.md)
- Unit tests (`tests/unit/test_agent.py`, 17; suite 144/144): search → answer, unique labels across searches, each limit, a result for every tool call over the limit, hard stop, bad / unparseable tool calls, doc filter on every tool, `read_chunk` caps, LLM error mid-loop, refusal, through the API
- Smoke test on Haiku (2026-10-19, 3 questions + 1 pipeline comparison, see agentic_ai.md §12): all correct; the agent narrowed a search to `services_fees.pdf` by itself; ~$0.001–0.003 per agent question vs ~$0.0005 pipeline. "Capital of France" scored 0.51 on `bsb.txt` (above `MIN_RELEVANCE` 0.35), so the hard stop didn't fire and the final call said not answerable
- Eval both modes on the M2 eval set (2026-10-21, Haiku, 4 runs ≈ $0.18; runner now reports `evidence_seen`, latency, cost, tool calls, stop reasons). **All docs:** pipeline false refusal 61% (HNSW bug) → agent **0%**, evidence seen 39% → 97%, quote pass 100% and correct refusal 100% in both. **Own doc:** both modes 0% false refusal / 100% correct refusal. Agent cost $0.0021 vs $0.0004 per question (all docs; $0.0013 vs $0.0005 own doc), latency median 5.9 s vs 1.3 s, 2.7 tool calls/question (3/42 hit the limit). Full table: agentic_ai.md §13, design doc Appendix D
- Default `QA_MODE`: **keep `pipeline`** (user's decision, 2026-10-26). After `rebuild-index` both modes meet §12 on all docs; agent costs ~2.6× and is ~4× slower for +8 pts follow-ups and −2 pts false refusal (M2 results above), which the $5 API budget doesn't justify. `QA_MODE=agent` stays available
- UI: agent steps as status lines (2026-10-21). Backend: `steps` on the reply and on each assistant message in `GET /conversations/{id}` (from `qa_trace_steps`; tool result summaries now carry `filename` + `page`). Notes after the last tool call are left out: Haiku's closing note restates the answer, unverified. Frontend: `utils/steps.ts` (`stepLine`, `stepsSummary`; 7 Vitest tests), collapsible "2 searches, 1 read" list in `AnswerMessage` (plain text, no HTML). Shown after the answer arrives; live status while it runs needs M4 SSE `status` events. Checked in the browser on a scratch DB with real Haiku (reply + reload). Unit tests 149/149, Vitest 28/28
- README + §2.3: more chunks per question may be sent to Anthropic (every search result the agent reads) (2026-10-21; README also gets a "Q&A modes" section)

## M4 — Conversation (done 2026-10-22, branch `conversation` on top of `token-budget`)

Unit tests 191/191, Vitest 31/31. Smoke-tested on a scratch DB with real Haiku (curl SSE in both modes, follow-ups, a document summary) and in the browser (live status, "Searched for", summary dialog). Design doc v2.4, Appendix E.

- Follow-up question condensing (`generation/conversation.py`): with earlier turns, one Claude call (`StandaloneQuestion`, stage `condense`) rewrites the question; only the standalone question is searched and answered, in both modes (the agent gets it too, so no separate "agent writes its own queries" path). Saved on the user message (`standalone_question`) and in `qa_traces.standalone_question`; the reply returns it; the UI shows "Searched for: …" under the question. Condense failure = 503 like other LLM errors, the question is kept; a blank rewrite falls back to the original
- Chat history: the last `HISTORY_TURNS` (6) question/answer pairs, answers cut to `HISTORY_ANSWER_CHARS` (800); failed questions (no answer) left out; history wrapped as data in the prompt (`</conversation>` escaped)
- SSE streaming: `Accept: text/event-stream` on `POST /conversations/{id}/messages` (JSON stays the default for tests and eval). Worker thread + queue; events `status` (condensing / condensed / retrieving / searching / tool_call / answering / verifying), `token`, `sources` (= the JSON reply), `done`, `error`. Tokens are the `answer` field read from the partial structured JSON (`LangChainChatModel.stream_structured`); none in `STRICT_MODE`. A client disconnect doesn't stop the answer from being saved. UI: live status line, streamed text greyed until `sources` replaces it, abort on conversation switch
- Conversation summaries: when more than `HISTORY_TURNS` pairs are pending, the oldest are folded into `conversations.summary` (≤ 150 words, stage `summary`, keeps half the window as pairs), so roughly one extra call every 3 questions in long chats. A failed fold is logged and the question is still answered
- Document summaries (F6), on request: `GET/POST /documents/{id}/summary`, map-reduce with verified quote points (`generation/summary.py`), own job queue, interrupted jobs marked failed on startup, cost estimate shown on the button and checked against the budget (429), tokens in the new `llm_usage` table so they count toward `DAILY_BUDGET_USD` (`/usage` days now have `summaries`). Library: book icon → `SummaryDialog`. services_fees.pdf: 7 points, ~$0.003 (estimate $0.0025)
